        "question_text": "Name the hypotenuse in each triangle.\n(a)\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]\n\\usetikzlibrary{calc}\n\\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (B) at (3.4,0);\n\\coordinate (C) at (0,2.2);\n\\draw[black] (A)--(B) node[midway,below,text=black] {$p$};\n\\draw[black] (A)--(C) node[midway,left,text=black] {$q$};\n\\draw[black] (B)--(C) node[midway,above right,text=black] {$r$};\n\\coordinate (ra) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(B)$);\n\\coordinate (rb) at ($(A)!0.3cm!(C)$);\n\\draw[black] (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(A)$)--(rb);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]\n(b)\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]\n\\usetikzlibrary{calc}\n\\coordinate (D) at (0,2);\n\\coordinate (E) at (-2.8,0.4);\n\\coordinate (F) at (0.8,0.6);\n\\draw[black] (D)--(E)--(F)--cycle;\n\\node[above,text=black] at (D) {$D$};\n\\node[below left,text=black] at (E) {$E$};\n\\node[below right,text=black] at (F) {$F$};\n\\coordinate (ra) at ($(D)!0.3cm!(E)$);\n\\coordinate (rb) at ($(D)!0.3cm!(F)$);\n\\draw[black] (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(D)$)--(rb);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]",
        "solution_text": "(a) $r$, opposite the marked right angle.\n(b) $EF$, opposite the right angle at $D$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "This triangle is right-angled. The right angle is not marked.\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]\n\\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (B) at (3,0);\n\\coordinate (C) at (0,3.15);\n\\draw[black] (A)--(B) node[midway,below,text=black] {$20\\text{ cm}$};\n\\draw[black] (A)--(C) node[midway,left,text=black] {$21\\text{ cm}$};\n\\draw[black] (B)--(C) node[midway,above right,text=black] {$29\\text{ cm}$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]\nWhich side length is the hypotenuse?",
        "solution_text": "$29$ cm, the longest side of this right-angled triangle."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "A loading ramp joins level ground to a platform. The vertical rise and the ground meet at a right angle. Which length is the hypotenuse?\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black}]\n\\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\n\\coordinate (C) at (0,2);\n\\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,left] {rise};\n\\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {ground};\n\\draw (C)--(B) node[midway,sloped,above] {ramp};\n\\draw (0,0.25)--(0.25,0.25)--(0.25,0);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]",
        "solution_text": "The sloping length of the ramp is the hypotenuse, opposite the right angle between the rise and the ground."
      }
